      "title": "Violent protests and killings in Bangladesh ahead of exiled Sheikh Hasina’s planned return",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/19/bangladesh-violent-protest-sheikh-hasina-planned-return",
      "description": "<p>Awami League party called for ⁠nationwide protest on Thursday after the government rejected Hasina’s request for passport</p><p>Parts of Bangladesh were shut down Thursday as protests by supporters of former prime minister Sheikh Hasina sparked clashes, bomb blasts and arson attacks, with the ancestral home ⁠of former leader Muhammad Yunus set ablaze in the violence.</p><p>Hasina’s Awami League party had called for a ​week-long programme of protests and rallies to mobilise support ‌for <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/10/disgraced-former-leader-sheikh-hasina-plans-return-to-bangladesh-after-two-years-in-exile\">Hasina’s planned return in December</a>, culminating in a ‌nationwide lockdown on Thursday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/19/bangladesh-violent-protest-sheikh-hasina-planned-return\">Continue reading...</a>",
